WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.324
A literature review can fail before screening begins.

00:00:03.324 --> 00:00:12.466
If the population of eligible papers comes from changing portals, undocumented searches, or private exports, another researcher cannot reconstruct the same denominator.

00:00:12.466 --> 00:00:24.100
TopVenues turns that first step into an executable artifact: a declared cybersecurity corpus, a fixed local snapshot, and tools for inspecting every aggregate back down to individual records.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.804
This August 2026 release contains fourteen thousand eight hundred fifty-nine records from twenty declared venues, covering 2019 through 2026.

00:00:38.804 --> 00:00:44.365
Ninety-four point one percent have searchable abstracts, and every record has BibTeX.

00:00:44.365 --> 00:00:46.219
The snapshot is immutable.

00:00:46.219 --> 00:00:55.950
After installation, its manifest, database, tests, search, export, and web health check can all be verified offline with one reproduction command.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.547
Start in Search with a research question, not with a ranking.

00:01:04.547 --> 00:01:09.507
Here I search for L L M security using full-text BM25 ranking.

00:01:09.507 --> 00:01:12.400
The result is not a recommendation list.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:20.667
It is an inspectable candidate set: title, authors, venue, year, class, abstract preview, source link, and citation record remain visible.

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:24.800
Substring filters are also available when exact textual mention matters.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:40.620
For reference mapping, I can restrict the same question to the security top four: ACM CCS, IEEE Security and Privacy, USENIX Security, and NDSS.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.718
That returns seventy-eight records in this snapshot.

00:01:43.718 --> 00:01:50.355
A systematic review should normally begin with all venues unless its protocol justifies a restriction.

00:01:50.355 --> 00:01:56.550
Either way, the exact subset can be exported as CSV, JSON, or ready-to-cite BibTeX.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.957
Insights provides distributions, but the charts are not decorative.

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:08.793
Every venue, year, class, and coverage bar is a navigation control.

00:02:08.793 --> 00:02:14.509
Clicking a bar transfers its value into Search and opens the supporting records.

00:02:14.509 --> 00:02:25.500
That drill-down is important: a researcher can challenge an aggregate immediately, inspect outliers, and export the evidence instead of trusting a dashboard number without provenance.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.496
The topic view separates raw volume from share of each year's corpus.

00:02:34.496 --> 00:02:43.112
For L L M in the top four, it finds two hundred eighty-two papers, led by CCS, USENIX, NDSS, and Security and Privacy.

00:02:43.112 --> 00:02:47.233
The share curve prevents corpus growth from masquerading as topic growth.

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:55.850
And 2026 is visibly marked as partial, so this chart supports monitoring without pretending an incomplete year is comparable to a completed one.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.439
Researcher Radar answers three different questions.

00:03:02.439 --> 00:03:05.285
Any-author frequency shows recurring names across collaborations.

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:09.351
First-author frequency emphasizes who most often leads the author list.

00:03:09.351 --> 00:03:18.702
Last-author frequency can be useful in fields where that position often reflects group leadership, but the tool never assumes that convention is universal.

00:03:18.702 --> 00:03:24.800
Paper count is the transparent default; optional tier weighting is clearly labeled as a heuristic.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:39.684
Selecting a name opens the evidence behind the row: annual publication trajectory, first- and last-author positions, direct coauthors, active years, and main venues.

00:03:39.684 --> 00:03:43.895
DBLP identity suffixes are preserved to reduce accidental homonym merges.

00:03:43.895 --> 00:03:49.789
These views reveal whom to read and monitor within a declared topic and scope.

00:03:49.789 --> 00:03:54.000
They do not measure citations, seniority, authority, or scientific quality.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:08.071
For ongoing surveillance, download a portable watchlist containing the topic, authors, tier scope, and paper IDs already observed.

00:04:08.071 --> 00:04:12.107
A later snapshot can compute deterministic additions and removals.

00:04:12.107 --> 00:04:19.282
The emerging-activity table compares recent and earlier publication rates as a descriptive signal, not a forecast.

00:04:19.282 --> 00:04:28.250
The arXiv handoff searches an author's name for possible preprints; every match remains an unverified candidate until identity is checked.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.622
Evidence makes the claim boundary explicit.

00:04:32.622 --> 00:04:37.867
Sidnei Barbieri manually reviewed a deterministic, venue-stratified sample of two hundred records.

00:04:37.867 --> 00:04:44.860
One hundred sixty-nine abstracts satisfied all three criteria: complete, uncontaminated, and matched to the sampled paper.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:55.350
That is an eighty-four point five percent usable rate, with a ninety-five percent Wilson interval from seventy-eight point eight to eighty-eight point nine percent.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:12.466
The audit was performed on the previous snapshot and transferred only after an exact check showed the same fourteen thousand eight hundred fifty-nine paper IDs and identical abstract text.

00:05:12.466 --> 00:05:16.334
Version four changes ten titles, none in the sample.

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:21.922
Coverage is still uneven: for example, ESORICS and WOOT have substantial missing abstracts.

00:05:21.922 --> 00:05:28.800
Missing text is disclosed and excluded from abstract-dependent conclusions; it is never treated as negative evidence.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.645
Dataset lifecycle separates exploration from maintenance.

00:05:32.645 --> 00:05:36.171
A released profile cannot be refreshed in place.

00:05:36.171 --> 00:05:47.631
New collection from live APIs must create a successor profile, record provenance, compare added and removed IDs, rerun quality gates, and receive a new semantic release.

00:05:47.631 --> 00:05:52.479
On Linux and macOS, reproduce dot sh exercises the reviewer path.

00:05:52.479 --> 00:05:58.650
Native Windows uses reproduce dot P S one and closes every SQLite handle deterministically.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.483
A productive workflow is therefore simple.

00:06:02.483 --> 00:06:05.380
Begin broad when constructing a systematic-review denominator.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:09.518
Narrow to the top four when mapping canonical security conversations.

00:06:09.518 --> 00:06:13.243
Inspect the records behind every trend or author signal.

00:06:13.243 --> 00:06:16.554
Export the candidate set with its snapshot identity.

00:06:16.554 --> 00:06:19.451
Save a watchlist for the next release.

00:06:19.451 --> 00:06:26.900
And document each restriction as a protocol choice, because TopVenues supports scientific judgment; it does not replace it.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:41.346
TopVenues gives researchers three things that ordinary search portals do not provide together: a reproducible denominator, an inspectable research workbench, and a forward-looking monitoring handoff.

00:06:41.346 --> 00:06:52.238
The code, immutable corpus, audit evidence, documentation, and seven-minute demonstration are published with release one point five point zero on GitHub and Hugging Face.

00:06:52.238 --> 00:06:59.500
Reproduce the snapshot, challenge the claims, and build the review from evidence you can carry forward.
